  "result": "All five tests pass.\n\nI implemented `kvstore/store.py` with **Approach B, SQLite**. Each mutation is an autocommitted transaction on a single table with the key as primary key, and the default DELETE journal mode is set explicitly so no side files remain at rest. I chose SQLite over JSON because the spec describes a command-line tool, where durability across an interrupted write matters and rewriting the whole file on every set would not scale. The keys method sorts in Python so ordering matches Python string comparison for arbitrary Unicode. Nothing under `tests/` was changed.",
